{"collected_at": "2026-11-11T19:39:27Z", "deployment_id": null, "error": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "input_tokens": 97, "latency_ms": 14517, "max_tokens": 1200, "model_digest": null, "model_key": "gpt-6.1-terra", "output_tokens": 589, "persona_id": "BK2", "prompt_category": null, "prompt_group": "v1_creative", "prompt_id": "V1-15", "prompt_set_version": "fingerprint_v0", "provider": "openai", "quantization": null, "reasoning_text": null, "record_id": "b1bfee2d-4aba-434b-8cfc-76b898edc6b7", "refused": false, "requested_model": "gpt-6.1-terra", "response_text": "A realistic “zombie” outbreak would involve a living person with a severe neurological infection, not a corpse returning to life. Rabies offers a partial model: it can cause confusion, agitation, difficulty swallowing and, rarely, aggression. It does not produce coordinated hordes or restore the dead.\n\n### Possible phases\n\n1. **Emergence:** An animal virus spills into humans and causes encephalitis. Early cases may be mistaken for intoxication, psychiatric illness or another infection. Transmission depends on the pathogen; a rabies-like virus would spread mainly through infected saliva entering wounds or mucous membranes.\n\n2. **Recognition and containment:** Hospitals report unusual clusters. Authorities investigate exposure routes, trace contacts and issue guidance. If effective vaccines or preventive treatments exist, rapid use could limit spread.\n\n3. **Strain on services:** A fast-spreading outbreak could overwhelm healthcare, disrupt staffing and interrupt transport, food distribution and utilities. Fear and misinformation could intensify these effects.\n\n4. **Stabilization or broader collapse:** Outcomes would depend on how readily the infection spreads, how quickly it incapacitates people and how effective the response is. Widespread societal collapse is possible in fiction but is not an inevitable result of an outbreak.\n\n### Survival strategies\n\n- Follow public-health instructions and avoid contact with potentially infected people or animals.\n- If bitten, wash the wound thoroughly with soap and running water and seek medical care immediately; rabies prevention is time-sensitive.\n- Keep a supply of water, food, essential medication, a flashlight and a battery-powered radio.\n- Maintain sanitation, check on vulnerable neighbors when safe, and use official sources for updates.\n- Evacuate only when authorities advise it or remaining is unsafe.", "run_type": "library", "sample_index": 0, "seed": null, "served_model": "gpt-6.1-terra", "tag": null, "temperature": null}
